# Testing — ls-toto

## Scope

The Makefile `test` target builds and runs **`build/tests/test_core`** (or
`build/tests/test_core.exe` on Windows).

Tests cover the **pure modules** — option parsing (`ls_toto_cli.c`), sorting
(`ls_toto_sort.c`), and formatting helpers (`ls_toto_format.c`) — on every
platform, plus **POSIX directory reading** via `opendir()` / `readdir()` when
the POSIX headers are available. They do **not** exercise `ls_toto_fs.c`, the
Win32 `FindFirstFileA` path, `ls_toto_list.c`, or the production `write()` to
stdout. There are **no** subprocess / integration tests in-tree.

When the build defines **`LS_TOTO_WIN32_FS`**, POSIX-only suites print
**`SKIP: <name>`** and return — `make test` still exits 0.

## Layout

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `tests/test_runner.c` | `main()` — invokes all suites in fixed order |
| `tests/test_out_stub.c` / `.h` | defines `ls_toto_out_*()` into an in-memory buffer so `ls_toto_format.c` links without `ls_toto_out.c`; the header exposes `test_out_stub_buffer()` / `test_out_stub_reset()` (the only pair without a `_run()` suite) |
| `tests/test_cli_parse.c` / `.h` | `ls_toto_parse_args()` flags, operands, meta flags, bad options |
| `tests/test_sort_order.c` / `.h` | name / mtime / size order and reverse |
| `tests/test_format_mode.c` / `.h` | `ls_toto_format_mode()` 10-char strings |
| `tests/test_format_size.c` / `.h` | `ls_toto_format_size_human()` rounding |
| `tests/test_fs_readdir.c` / `.h` | POSIX `opendir(".")` / `readdir()` sanity (`SKIP` on Win32) |

Order in `test_runner.c`: cli_parse → sort_order → format_mode → format_size →
fs_readdir.

One scenario per `.c` / `.h` pair; headers declare `void test_<module>_<name>_run(void)`.

Test objects and the linked binary live under **`build/tests/`** (not under
`tests/`).

## Framework

- No external framework — plain C with `<assert.h>`.
- Each case prints `PASS: <descriptive name>` on success.
- `assert()` failure → `abort()` → non-zero exit from `make test`.

## Build (from `Makefile`)

```makefile
TEST_CORE := $(TEST_BUILD_DIR)/test_core   # build/tests/test_core
TEST_LINKED_SRCS := src/ls_toto_cli.c src/ls_toto_sort.c src/ls_toto_format.c

$(TEST_CORE): $(TEST_OBJS) $(TEST_LINKED_OBJS) $(HDRS) $(TEST_HDRS) | $(TEST_BUILD_DIR)
	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) -o $@ $(TEST_OBJS) $(TEST_LINKED_OBJS)

test: $(TEST_CORE)
	./$(TEST_CORE)
```

Tests link **only** the pure modules (compiled into `build/tests/`), never
`src/main.c`, `src/ls_toto_fs.c`, `src/ls_toto_out.c`, `src/ls_toto_emit.c`,
or `src/ls_toto_list.c`. They receive the same release `CFLAGS` as the main
binary (including `LS_TOTO_WIN32_FS` when applicable).

## Required cases

1. **CLI parse:** `-la` sets long + all; `-h` sets human-readable (not help);
   `--help` with `--version` → `HELP`; `--v` alone → `VERSION`; `a -l b`
   compacts operands to `a`, `b` with long set (permutation); `-- -l` makes
   `-l` an operand; `-z` → `BAD_SHORT` with `'z'`; `--foo` → `BAD_LONG`;
   last of `-l` / `-1` and `-t` / `-S` wins.
2. **Sort order:** names `b`, `a`, `C` → `C`, `a`, `b` (`strcmp`); `-t` newest
   first with name tie-break; `-S` largest first with name tie-break; `-r`
   reverses each.
3. **Format mode:** DIR `0755` → `drwxr-xr-x`; REG `0644` → `-rw-r--r--`;
   LNK `0777` → `lrwxrwxrwx`; `04755` → `-rwsr-xr-x`; `04644` → `-rwSr--r--`;
   DIR `01777` → `drwxrwxrwt`.
4. **Format size:** `0` → `0`; `1023` → `1023`; `1024` → `1.0K`; `1025` →
   `1.1K`; `1536` → `1.5K`; `10240` → `10K`; `10241` → `11K`; `1572864` → `1.5M`.
5. **Readdir (POSIX only):** `opendir(".")` lists `.` and `..`;
   `opendir("does-not-exist")` returns NULL with `errno == ENOENT`.
   `SKIP: fs_readdir` under `LS_TOTO_WIN32_FS`.
6. Never call `exit()` from a test; use `assert()` or `return` only.

## Adding tests

- Add `tests/test_<module>_<name>.c` + `.h`, declare runner in `.h`, call from
  `test_runner.c`, append to `TEST_SRCS` in `Makefile`.
- Wrap POSIX-only code in `#ifndef LS_TOTO_WIN32_FS` with a `SKIP` stub in the
  `#else` branch.
- Keep tests allocation-free; stack buffers and string-literal entry names only.
- If a new pure module is tested, append it to `TEST_LINKED_SRCS`; never link
  modules that perform real I/O.

## Manual smoke tests (not automated)

After `make`:

```sh
./build/ls-toto                      # expect: names in ., no dotfiles, exit 0
./build/ls-toto -la                  # expect: total line, long format incl. . and .., exit 0
./build/ls-toto -lh build            # expect: human-readable sizes, exit 0
./build/ls-toto -R src               # expect: src: header, recursive sections, exit 0
./build/ls-toto -d src               # expect: src, exit 0
./build/ls-toto -F                   # expect: / on directories, * on executables, exit 0
./build/ls-toto | cat                # expect: one name per line, exit 0
./build/ls-toto missing              # expect: cannot access on stderr, exit 2
./build/ls-toto -z                   # expect: invalid option + hint on stderr, exit 2
./build/ls-toto --version            # expect: ls-toto <version>, exit 0
./build/ls-toto --help               # expect: usage text on stdout, exit 0
```
